# Line endings, decided by the file rather than by whoever checked it out.
#
# The shell scripts are the reason this file exists: a .sh checked out with CRLF fails on
# Linux with an error that names the wrong thing entirely ("bad interpreter"), and the
# scripts exist precisely so Linux users can build. Batch files want the opposite.
* text=auto

*.sh     text eol=lf
*.bash   text eol=lf
*.bat    text eol=crlf
*.cmd    text eol=crlf

# The JavaScript preludes are embedded as the bytes of the file, so the file has to be the
# same bytes however it was checked out: with autocrlf on Windows it would otherwise be a
# different prelude there than on Linux.
RendeerAlpha/toolchain/src/Layout/js/*.js text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to "fix" them.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.rdab   binary
*.lib    binary
